  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 205 PM CDT Thu May 7 2026\n\nFriday night through Thursday:\n\nSome moderation in temperatures are expected Friday and Saturday\nwith temperatures closer to normal for this time of year with\nreadings in the 60s to near 70. There is still a chance of \nshowers on Saturday, although the models diverge on what part of\nthe state would see the highest chances of rain. Behind the \nsystem on Saturday, gusty west to northwest winds are expected \nwhich will usher in cooler temperatures for Sunday and Monday. \nIt is possible that some of the area would see frost again \nSunday night, prompting another night of Frost Advisories. The\nnext significant chance (50-70%) of rain arrives late Monday \nnight and continues into Tuesday evening. It appears by the\nmiddle of next week, temperatures should be at or slightly above\nnormal\n\nEckberg\nWFO MKX",
